1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,281
Release Scribe is a Forge app.

2
00:00:02,401 --> 00:00:07,056
The manifest registers a Jira project page and a Rovo agent with two
actions.

3
00:00:07,176 --> 00:00:10,520
The notes engine is plain TypeScript in src/core.

4
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:15,818
Next, the offline demo drafts version 1.4.0 from sample issues.

5
00:00:15,938 --> 00:00:18,806
This repository has not been installed on a site.

6
00:00:20,023 --> 00:00:25,677
Release Scribe turns a Jira fix version into notes for engineering,
customers, and executives.

7
00:00:25,797 --> 00:00:28,444
This pass uses sample issues in the repo.

8
00:00:28,564 --> 00:00:31,722
Nothing is signed in, and no request leaves the machine.

9
00:00:31,842 --> 00:00:35,662
Atlas Board, key A T L A S.

10
00:00:35,782 --> 00:00:39,125
Unreleased version 1.4.0 sorts first.

11
00:00:40,078 --> 00:00:42,493
The app prints the query before it searches.

12
00:00:42,613 --> 00:00:47,977
Project Atlas, fix version 1.4.0, ordered by issue type and key.

13
00:00:48,097 --> 00:00:51,080
The project page and the Rovo action share this helper.

14
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:54,115
On a live site the query runs as the person who asked.

15
00:00:55,078 --> 00:00:58,526
The fixture matches a Jira search split across two pages.

16
00:00:58,646 --> 00:01:04,451
Ten issues parse into three features, two improvements, two bug
fixes, and three other changes.

17
00:01:04,571 --> 00:01:06,545
Tasks and a spike stay under Other.

18
00:01:06,665 --> 00:01:09,683
Page two is how a next page token comes back.

19
00:01:11,095 --> 00:01:14,903
Engineering notes keep the key, the status, and the priority.

20
00:01:15,023 --> 00:01:19,063
The guest link story still shows its internal tag and feat prefix.

21
00:01:19,183 --> 00:01:20,739
That is the original summary.

22
00:01:20,859 --> 00:01:24,748
Asterisks in the drag and drop title are escaped so they stay
literal.

23
00:01:26,110 --> 00:01:28,409
Customer notes drop keys and status.

24
00:01:28,529 --> 00:01:32,639
Square-bracket tags and prefixes such as feat, fix, and chore come
off.

25
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:36,079
The guest link line reads, Share a board with a guest link.

26
00:01:36,199 --> 00:01:39,206
The query text stays in the engineering section only.

27
00:01:41,125 --> 00:01:43,563
The executive summary is one paragraph.

28
00:01:43,683 --> 00:01:47,224
It counts each group and names three highlights from the front of
the list.

29
00:01:47,344 --> 00:01:48,935
No language model wrote it.

30
00:01:49,055 --> 00:01:51,946
The same issues always produce the same sentence.

31
00:01:52,066 --> 00:01:54,248
You can see the counts match the groups above.

32
00:01:55,214 --> 00:01:57,815
The Markdown file stacks all three sections.

33
00:01:57,935 --> 00:02:02,335
It is saved under demo output as ATLAS 1.4.0 markdown.

34
00:02:02,455 --> 00:02:07,018
Engineering, customer, and the executive paragraph are all in that
file.

35
00:02:07,138 --> 00:02:12,861
The timestamp is 9 November 2026, so every run matches this
recording.

36
00:02:13,830 --> 00:02:18,010
The other action asks what changed since version 1.3.0.

37
00:02:18,130 --> 00:02:21,288
The query uses fix versions ordered after that baseline.

38
00:02:21,408 --> 00:02:27,793
This sample returns the 1.3.1 calendar fix, the guest link, and the
drag and drop crash.

39
00:02:27,913 --> 00:02:30,850
The executive audience is the paragraph only.

40
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:34,363
Publish would send a Confluence storage page.

41
00:02:34,483 --> 00:02:38,337
The title includes the date, and the script tag is escaped to text.

42
00:02:38,457 --> 00:02:41,174
This demo builds the payload and does not send it.

43
00:02:41,294 --> 00:02:43,953
Release Scribe has not been installed on a site yet.

44
00:02:44,073 --> 00:02:46,011
The deploy steps are in the readme.

